// An `@html { … }` expression-tier block whose tier is declared in a *sibling* module (expr-tiers
// ∘ namespaced-types): importing the handler `render` brings its `@tier(html, …)` declaration into
// scope, so the block resolves and desugars to `Tmpl.render(statics, holes)`. Verifies the tier's
// `expr:` type qualifies in lockstep with the handler's return type, and that the handler's
// internal `wrap` helper is dragged into the merged program.
// expect: stdout "greeting:  hi [Ada]! "
// expect: exit 0

use Tmpl.{render, Html};

who = "Ada"
doc = @html { hi ${who}! }
echo "greeting: ${doc.text}"
